&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;There shall be no moving images, animation, video or full motion images displayed on the approved signs. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt; 
Reason: To ensure advertisements do not become a distraction, in the interests of the pedestrian and 
highway safety and to comply with Policy D8 of the London Plan 2021 and with Policy D12.7 of the Merton 
Local Plan 2024.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;In accordance with the categorisations set out in the ILP Guide PLG 05/23, the maximum nighttime 
luminance of the displays shall not exceed 300cd/m2 between the hours of 20:00 and 08:00 on any day. 
The maximum daylight luminance of the display shall not exceed 5,000cd/m2 outside of the above 
mentioned hours on any day. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify; &quot;&gt; 
Reason: To safeguard local amenity, prevent unnecessary light pollution, and ensure energy efficiency, in 
accordance with Policy D8 of the London Plan 2021 and with Policy D12.7 of the Merton Local Plan 2024&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

